Mplus VERSION 8.5
MUTHEN & MUTHEN
10/15/2025   2:27 PM

INPUT INSTRUCTIONS

  TITLE:	 generated dataset for 1-1-1 multilevel mediation
  	with cross-level interaction, no random cov. structure
  DATA:
   FILE = "example1crep1.dat";
  VARIABLE:
  		names are w y x m id;
  !		within = x;
  		between = w;
  		cluster = id;

  ANALYSIS:
  TYPE = TWOLEVEL RANDOM;
  ESTIMATOR = BAYES;


  		
  model:
  %within%
  ! mediation with random parameters
  sa | m on x;
  sb | y on m;
  scprime | y on x;

  %between%
  ! intercepts of random slopes
  [sa] (ma);
  [sb] (mb);
  [scprime] (mc);

  ! between-level mediation effects
  y ON m;
  m on x;
  y on x;

  ! cross-level interaction for sa (first stage mediation)
  [w]; w;
  w with x;
  m on w;
  sa on w;
  m with sa;

  MODEL CONSTRAINT:
  	NEW(indi);
  	indi = ma*mb;

  output:
  		tech9;



*** WARNING in MODEL command
  In the MODEL command, the x variable on the WITHIN level has been turned into a
  y variable to enable latent variable decomposition.  This variable will be treated
  as a y-variable on both levels:  X
*** WARNING in OUTPUT command
  TECH9 option is only available with Monte Carlo, multiple imputation or
  bootstrap.  Request for TECH9 is ignored.
   2 WARNING(S) FOUND IN THE INPUT INSTRUCTIONS



